# ouroboros#147 / t307: a DECOY, not a library. It shadows the stdlib's
# lib/bcd.eigs at step 2 of the VM's chain for a load issued from THIS
# directory (aot/test, the harness's main-file directory) and defines
# nothing. data/lf147_sub/stdlib_child.eigs loads "lib/bcd.eigs" from ITS
# directory, where the chain ends at the stdlib root; a splicer that left
# that literal as a runtime call inside the native program would re-run
# the chain from the baked MAIN directory and load this file instead --
# printing the line below, then dying on `from_bcd`. Do not load this file
# from a depth-0 fixture (both sides would agree on the decoy, vacuously).
print of "MAIN-DIR-BCD-SHADOW"
